{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "פתוח", :translit "patuach", :gloss "open"} {:he "וכל כלי פתוח", :translit "vechol kli patuach", :gloss "and every open vessel"} {:he "שרשי פתוח אלי מים", :translit "shorashei patuach elai mayim", :gloss "their roots open to me water"} {:he "קבר פתוח גרונם", :translit "kever patuach gronam", :gloss "an open grave their throat"} {:he "אשפתו כקבר פתוח", :translit "aspatotav kekever patuach", :gloss "his refuse-heaps like an open grave"} {:he "ד' מדות בכלי חרס", :translit "arba middot bichli cheress", :gloss "four levels in an earthenware vessel"} {:he "שרשי פתוח אלי מים", :translit "shorashei patuach elai mayim", :gloss "their roots open to me water"} {:he "פתוח גרונם", :translit "patuach gronam", :gloss "open their throat"} {:he "אשפתו כקבר פתוח", :translit "aspatotav kekever patuach", :gloss "his refuse-heaps like an open grave"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["וכל כלי פתוח" "שרשי פתוח אלי מים" "קבר פתוח גרונם" "אשפתו כקבר פתוח"]} {:kind :other, :note "Four escalating levels of perforation in an earthenware vessel mapped to the four Masorah occurrences of פתוח"}], :frame {:text "Mishnah Kelim 3:2-7 defines four degrees of perforation in an earthenware vessel, each progressively disqualifying it from a different function. The first level: a hole that lets liquid enter means it can no longer sanctify hatat water (Kelim 3:2). The vessel retains capacity for seeds: a planter whose hole is the size of a small root still holds seeds planted in it without receiving impurity, per the rule in Mishnah Kelim 3:6 that a perforated planter does not contract impurity. The next level: a hole large enough for an olive to exit relates to ordinary eating, since the halakhic measure for eating is an olive's volume (Kelim 3:6). The final level: a hole large enough for a pomegranate to exit renders the vessel useless, thrown to the garbage (Kelim 3:6). The verse 'אשפתו כקבר פתוח' is from Isaiah 30:33; 'שרשי פתוח אלי מים' is from Job 8:11; 'קבר פתוח גרונם' is from Psalms 5:10.", :sources ["Mishnah Kelim 3:2" "Mishnah Kelim 3:6" "Mishnah Kelim 3:7" "Job 8:11" "Psalms 5:10" "Isaiah 30:33"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["וכל כלי פתוח" "שרשי פתוח אלי מים" "קבר פתוח גרונם" "אשפתו כקבר פתוח"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וכל כלי פתוח", :refs ["Numbers 19:15"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "שרשי פתוח אלי מים", :refs ["Job 29:19"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "קבר פתוח גרונם", :refs ["Psalms 5:10"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "אשפתו כקבר פתוח", :refs ["Jeremiah 5:16"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Four escalating levels of perforation in an earthenware vessel mapped to the four Masorah occurrences of פתוח", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:06.802446840Z", :model "glm-5.2"}